Ontology,Realism,"Realism holds that the world has a stable structure that exists independently of human observation or interpretation. Reality is 'out there' waiting to be discovered through systematic investigation. Gameplay Effect: +2 points if your stack includes a Method with Reproducibility 8 or higher.",,,,
Ontology,Relativism,"Relativism argues that what we call 'reality' changes with culture, language, and history. Truth is relative to social, cultural, and historical contexts. Gameplay Effect: +2 points if your stack includes Methods from different paradigms (e.g., one with Reproducibility 7+ and one with Sensibility 7+).",,,,
Ontology,Constructivism,"Constructivism sees reality as something people actively build together through conversation, symbols, shared practices, and social interaction. What we call 'reality' is socially constructed. Gameplay Effect: When you complete a stack with 2+ Methods with Sensibility 7+, draw 1 card (then discard to 7).",,,,
Ontology,Critical Realism,"Critical Realism combines realist ontology with interpretive epistemology. Reality exists independently but can only be known through human interpretation and is stratified into layers. Bridges quantitative and qualitative approaches. Gameplay Effect: +3 points if your stack includes Methods with both high Reproducibility (6+) and high Sensibility (6+).",,,,
Ontology,Relational Ontology,"Relational Ontology sees reality as existing in relationships rather than isolated entities. Emphasizes interconnection, process, and context. Central to Indigenous philosophies and ecological thinking. Gameplay Effect: +3 points if your stack includes Participatory Methods, Action Research, or Ethnography.",,,,
Epistemology,Positivism,"Compatible Ontology: Realism, Critical Realism. Incompatible Ontology: Relativism, Constructivism, Relational Ontology.","Survey (Quantitative), Experimental Design, Statistical Analysis, Content Analysis, Social Media Mining, Archival Research, Corpus Linguistics",,,,
Epistemology,Interpretivism,"Compatible Ontology: Relativism, Constructivism, Critical Realism, Relational Ontology. Incompatible Ontology: None.","Interview (Qualitative), Case Study, Ethnography, Textual Analysis, Oral History, Biographical Method, Thematic Analysis",,,,
Epistemology,Critical Epistemology,"Compatible Ontology: Realism, Constructivism, Critical Realism, Relational Ontology. Incompatible Ontology: None.","Discourse Analysis, Critical Discourse Analysis, Action Research, Participatory Methods, Ethnography",,,,
Epistemology,Feminist Epistemology,"Compatible Ontology: Relativism, Constructivism, Relational Ontology. Incompatible Ontology: Realism, Positivism.","Autoethnography, Narrative Inquiry, Participatory Methods, Creative Writing as Inquiry, Memory-Work Method",,,,
Epistemology,Constructivist Epistemology,"Compatible Ontology: Relativism, Constructivism, Critical Realism, Relational Ontology. Incompatible Ontology: None.","Grounded Theory, Ethnography, Interview (Qualitative), Focus Groups",,,,
Epistemology,Embodied Epistemology,"Compatible Ontology: Relativism, Constructivism, Relational Ontology. Incompatible Ontology: Realism.","Performance Ethnography, Walking Interview, Embodied Mapping, Soundwalk Method, Phenomenology, Sensory Ethnography",,,,
Epistemology,Aesthetic Epistemology,"Compatible Ontology: Relativism, Constructivism, Relational Ontology. Incompatible Ontology: Realism, Critical Realism.","Practice-Based Research, Film Analysis, VR Ethnography, Drawing as Inquiry, Performance Ethnography, Sensory Ethnography",,,,
Epistemology,Pragmatist,"Compatible Ontology: All (Realism, Relativism, Constructivism, Critical Realism, Relational Ontology). Incompatible Ontology: None.","Mixed-Methods Research, Focus Groups, Action Research, Digital Humanities Methods, Speculative Design, Cultural Probes",,,,
Epistemology,Objectivism,"Compatible Ontology: Realism, Critical Realism. Incompatible Ontology: Constructivism, Relativism, Relational Ontology.","Experimental Design, Survey (Quantitative), Statistical Analysis, Content Analysis, Semiotic Analysis",,,,
