Method,Sensory Ethnography,"Ethnographic approach emphasizing non-visual senses (sound, smell, touch, taste) in understanding culture and experience.","Embodied, Aesthetic",,7,3,9,7
Method,Usability Testing,"Evaluating products or interfaces by testing them with representative users to identify usability problems and gather feedback.","Pragmatist, Design",,5,7,6,6
Method,Iconographic Analysis,"Study of symbolism, allegory, and meaning in visual art. Identifies and interprets subject matter and symbolic content of images.","Interpretivism, Art History",,2,6,7,4
Method,Stylistic Analysis,"Analysis of formal visual qualities such as line, color, composition, and technique to understand artistic style and attribution.","Objectivism, Art History",,1,7,5,3
Method,Social Network Analysis,"Mapping and measuring relationships and flows between people, groups, organizations, or other connected entities. Uses graph theory and visualization.","Positivism, Digital",,3,8,4,7
Method,Q-Methodology,"Systematic study of subjectivity and viewpoints. Participants sort statements according to their perspective, analyzed using factor analysis.","Constructivist, Social Science",,4,7,6,7
Method,Meta-Analysis,"Statistical technique combining results from multiple independent studies to identify overall patterns and estimate effect sizes.","Positivism, Realism",,2,9,2,5
Method,Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT),"Experimental design where participants are randomly assigned to treatment or control groups. Gold standard for establishing causation.","Positivism, Realism",,7,10,1,4
Method,Close Reading,"Careful, sustained interpretation of a brief passage of text. Emphasizes attention to language, structure, and meaning.","Interpretivism, Humanities",,1,5,8,2
Method,Distant Reading,"Computational analysis of large text corpora using algorithms. Identifies patterns across thousands of texts impossible to read individually.","Positivism, Digital Humanities",,1,8,3,8
Method,Topic Modeling,"Computational method discovering abstract topics in text collections using algorithms like Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA).","Positivism, Digital Humanities",,1,8,3,9
Method,Conversation Analysis,"Micro-analysis of talk-in-interaction. Studies the sequential organization of conversation including turn-taking, repair, and action formation.","Interpretivism, Social Science",,6,7,7,5
Method,Life History Method,"In-depth biographical research collecting individual life stories to understand lived experience and social-historical contexts.","Interpretivism, Feminist",,6,4,8,4
Method,Photo Voice,"Participatory method where community members use photography to document and communicate their experiences and concerns.","Feminist, Participatory, Critical",,6,4,8,7
Method,Journey Mapping,"Visualization of user or customer experience over time, mapping touchpoints, emotions, and pain points across an entire service or process.","Pragmatist, Design",,3,6,6,6
Method,Prototyping as Method,"Using iterative prototype creation as a research tool to explore possibilities, test assumptions, and generate knowledge through making.","Pragmatist, Design, Aesthetic",,3,5,7,8
Method,Comparative Visual Analysis,"Systematic comparison of visual artworks, objects, or images to identify similarities, differences, patterns, and relationships.","Interpretivism, Art History",,1,6,6,4
Method,Reception Studies,"Study of how audiences, readers, or viewers interpret and respond to texts, artworks, or cultural objects across time and contexts.","Interpretivism, Critical",,5,5,7,5
Method,Regression Analysis,"Statistical method modeling relationships between dependent and independent variables to predict outcomes and estimate effects.","Positivism, Realism",,2,9,2,4
Method,Data Visualization,"Creating visual representations (charts, graphs, maps, diagrams) of data to reveal patterns, relationships, and insights.","Pragmatist, Digital",,2,7,5,7
Method,Co-Design,"Collaborative design process where researchers, designers, and stakeholders work together as equal partners throughout the design process.","Pragmatist, Participatory, Design",,5,5,7,7
Method,Systematic Review,"Comprehensive, structured review identifying and evaluating all available evidence on a research question using explicit, replicable methods.","Positivism, Critical",,2,9,4,5
Method,A/B Testing,"Experimental method comparing two versions (A and B) to determine which performs better. Common in digital design and marketing.","Positivism, Pragmatist, Design",,3,8,3,6
Method,Card Sorting,"Technique for understanding how users categorize and organize information. Reveals mental models and informs information architecture.","Pragmatist, Design",,3,7,5,5
Method,Diary Study,"Participants document experiences, activities, or thoughts over time in structured logs. Captures in-situ experiences and longitudinal patterns.","Interpretivism, Design",,5,5,7,6
Method,Contextual Inquiry,"Field research method combining observation and interview. Researchers observe users in their natural environment while asking questions.","Interpretivism, Pragmatist, Design",,6,6,7,5
Method,Think-Aloud Protocol,"Users verbalize thoughts, feelings, and decision processes while performing tasks. Reveals cognitive processes and usability issues.","Pragmatist, Design",,4,7,6,5
Method,Connoisseurship,"Art historical method based on expert judgment, experience, and intuition to determine attribution, authenticity, quality, and dating of artworks.","Art History, Aesthetic",,3,3,9,2
Method,Provenance Research,"Tracing the ownership history, custody, and geographic movement of artworks or objects. Essential for attribution and legal issues.","Art History, Historical",,4,7,5,3
Method,Technical Art History,"Scientific analysis of artworks using methods like X-ray, infrared, microscopy to study materials, techniques, and conservation.","Art History, Positivism",,2,9,4,6
Method,Factor Analysis,"Statistical method identifying underlying structures (factors) in multivariate data. Reduces complexity by grouping correlated variables.","Positivism, Social Science",,2,9,2,4
Method,Delphi Method,"Structured expert consensus technique using iterative rounds of anonymous surveys. Builds agreement on complex issues.","Pragmatist, Social Science",,4,7,5,5
Method,Quasi-Experimental Design,"Research design comparing groups without full random assignment. More practical than RCTs but with less internal validity.","Positivism, Social Science",,6,7,4,5
Method,Video Analysis,"Systematic analysis of video recordings to study behavior, interaction, practice, or performance. Allows repeated viewing and micro-analysis.","Interpretivism, Digital",,6,6,7,6
Method,GIS/Spatial Analysis,"Geographic Information Systems for collecting, managing, analyzing, and visualizing spatial and geographic data.","Positivism, Digital",,3,8,4,7
Method,Sentiment Analysis,"Computational analysis of text to identify and extract subjective information, especially emotional tone and opinion.","Positivism, Digital",,3,8,3,7
